# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Vulkan GPU tests (Linux).
#
# Mesa's RADV leaks a small block from a driver thread's one-time init
# (pthread_once). The loader unloads the driver when the last instance is
# destroyed, so the stack shows only "<unknown module>" frames under
# __pthread_once and cannot be matched by library name. Reproduced 2026-10-10
# with a bare volk program (create instance, enumerate GPUs, destroy) and Mesa
# 26.2.2: no RI code involved. RI does not call pthread_once/std::call_once.
leak:__pthread_once
